# Dart Basics

- Dart is a client-optimized programming language developed by Google.
- Dart became popular after it was adopted by Flutter.
- Dart can be used to build mobile, web, server and backend applications, e.g., Google Ads is built with Dart.
- Dart is an object-oriented language with C-style syntax, similar to Java, JavaScript and C#.
- Dart is fast and efficient because it supports both compilation modes:
  - **JIT (Just-in-Time):** used during development, enables hot reload.
  - **AOT (Ahead-of-Time):** used for release builds, gives fast app performance.

## Flutter

- Flutter is a UI framework that uses Dart.
- An app built with Flutter runs on both Android and iOS from a single codebase.

